              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for darkness, then the Marathi for to light up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: नळ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नळ — naḷ — \"a faucet; a water pipe\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आज सकाळपासून नळाला पाणी नाही. āj sakāḷpāsūn naḷālā pāṇī nāhī. There has been no water in the tap since this morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The tap takes -ला: नळाला पाणी येतं, water comes in the tap."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नळ (naḷ) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Marathi naḷ, \"lotus stalk; pipe, conduit\", under Sanskrit naḍa, \"a reed\" (CDIAL 6936): a hollow stalk and a pipe share one shape."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
